mode: "100644"
text: "# The REUSE framework — recycle the insight, not the artifact\n\nMost accounts treat content as disposable: publish once, never again — wasting their best assets.\nREUSE turns proven evergreen content into multiple cycles, **refreshed each time** so it's a new asset\n(not a stale duplicate Meta's 2026 rules would throttle).\n\n## R — Resurface the winners\n- Audit **native analytics** for proven evergreen pieces (by goal: engagement → saves/shares/comments;\n  traffic → CTR; growth → follows/mentions). Include **strong-but-underseen** posts that deserved more.\n- Keep only **evergreen** — exclude events, seasonal promos, dated news, trend-jacks.\n- Maintain a **recycling library/vault** (see the system reference) so winners are easy to re-queue.\n\n## E — Earn the slot again (refresh)\n- **Recycle the insight, not the artifact.** Give it a new hook, angle, or format (carousel → Reel →\n  text → quote card). **Change one major variable** per variant (hook / proof / CTA).\n- **Never repeat the same opening line.** Rewrite the first sentence, swap the opening visual, tighten\n  the first five seconds. Treat it as **editing, not duplication.**\n\n## U — Update for now\n- Verify **facts, stats, dates, prices, links** are still current — refresh anything outdated before\n  recycling. (A two-year-old \"algorithm\" or \"pricing\" post is often wrong now.)\n- Re-check **compliance/endorsement** language. **Disclose** any AI-refreshed media.\n\n## S — Schedule the cycle\n- Space each asset roughly **every 90–120 days**; don't dump a backlog. Sprinkle recycled pieces among\n  native new content.\n- Adapt to the **destination platform** (native format beats a copy-paste). Respect Meta's originality\n  rules — refreshed, not identical.\n\n## E — Evaluate & re-queue\n- Read native analytics on each cycle: which **variant** won, which asset earns another round.\n- Run **controlled tests** (one variable at a time) — one clean experiment beats a month of random\n  republishing. Promote winners back into the queue; retire the rest.\n\n## The recycling brief a request should fill\n```\nRESURFACE: which proven evergreen asset (+ its native metric) — and why now\nREFRESH: new hook / format / variable changed; first line + visual rewritten\nUPDATE: facts/stats/dates/prices/links verified current; compliance re-checked\nSCHEDULE: ~90–120-day spacing; destination platform + native format\nEVALUATE: which metric to watch; one-variable test; re-queue rule\n```\n\n> Not REUSE's job: same-moment multi-platform adaptation → **cross-platform-repurposing**;\n> long-form → short clips → **captions-and-clipping**; calendar/planning → **content-calendar**.\n"
